meta {
  name: verify email sent (name holder)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

get {
  url: {{base_url}}/rest-auth/registration/account-confirm-email/
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  ## API explanation
  **Do not call this.** It is listed only so the collection covers every route
  the server exposes.

  dj-rest-auth's `VerifyEmailView` is mounted here under the name
  `account_email_verification_sent`, which allauth reverses in parts of its
  signup flow. The route carries no `key` path segment, so a GET has nothing to
  confirm and returns **405**. The POST form of the same URL does work -- see
  **verify email (dj-rest-auth)** -- and is itself superseded by
  `POST /student/registration/verify-email/`.

  It stays mounted because deleting a URL name that a library reverses breaks the
  flow doing the reversing. That already happened once here: removing the
  `account_confirm_email` route made `send_email_confirmation()` raise, and
  signup emails silently stopped going out.

  ## API example response
  {
    "detail": "Method \"GET\" not allowed."
  }
}
